{"title":"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Turning a screwdriver <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> will drive a screw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27730c18d320bb116928056b0fc79e4511b325f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\text{ mm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> deeper into a piece of wood. How many complete revolutions are needed to drive the screw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0742680019b63ed7796c67129f951bc1f71557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 \\text{ mm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> into the wood?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6faff46841e27c104ee3340914e428e287fc12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A complete revolution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, so each complete revolution will drive the screw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150e2ccf347bc80b1618db0b4f1d2b959a0f20a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\text{ mm} \\times \\frac{360^{\\circ}}{90^{\\circ}} = 3 \\text { mm} \\times 4 = 12 \\text { mm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"279\" height=\"39\" /> deeper into the wood.\n</p><p>This means that the number of complete revolutions needed to drill <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0742680019b63ed7796c67129f951bc1f71557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 \\text{ mm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> into the wood would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0e1038f855aa30774f3660cbe53afa378dcd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36 \\text{ mm}}{12 \\text { mm}} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat\">1999 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><